.SH "نام (NAME)"
lr_spoold \- daemon, invoking lr_spool for all services periodically
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBlr_spoold\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBlr_spoold\fR is typically invoked from a init script after booting the system.
.PP
It should be started as
.PP
.Vb 1
\& lr_run lr_spoold
.Ve
.PP
under the Lire useraccount.  This is used to keep an online responder running.
See the "Responder Installation" section in the "Installing Lire" chapter of
the Lire User Manual for details.
.PP
\&\fBlr_spoold\fR invokes \fBlr_check_service\fR\|(1) to get a list of services, which are
used as addresses for an online responder. For each address \fR\f(CI$service\fR\fI\fR in this
list, it runs
.PP
.Vb 1
\&  lr_spool $spooldir lr_processmail $service
.Ve
.PP
periodically. \f(CW$spooldir\fR gets constructed using profile_lean and
the address.
.PP
Typically, spooldir is a Maildir\*(Aqs \`new\*(Aq subdirectory, like e.g.
.PP
.Vb 1
\& .../var/spool/lire/$address/Maildir/new/
.Ve
.PP
\&.
.PP
In effect, we make it possible to invoke lr_processmail with the right
arguments for each message, so that logfiles in the messages get processed
by the right 2dlf convertor.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBlr_spool\fR\|(1), \fBlr_processmail\fR\|(1)
